# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the L1 norm {#use-the-l1-norm}"
msgstr "Gamitin ang L1 norm {#use-the-l1-norm}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, and as you have already seen in the [Truncate Pauli terms](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms) guide, `p_norm=1`, which means that the error is estimated as:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle\\psi|\\Delta|\\psi\\rangle| \\leq \\sum_{P\\in\\mathcal{T}} |c_P|\n"
"$$\n"
"where $\\psi$ is the quantum state, $\\Delta$ is the real difference between the exact and truncated observable (which is unknown), $\\mathcal{T}$ is the set of Pauli terms that were truncated, and $c_P$ is the Pauli terms coefficient.\n"
"This inequality is a rigorous but very loose upper bound for most scenarios.\n"
"This guide, backpropagates six slices of the example circuit, using a constant error per slice of `0.001`. This value is to be understood as the budget within the given `p_norm`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang default, at gaya ng nakita mo na sa gabay na [Truncate Pauli terms](/addons/qiskit-addon-obp/guides/truncate-operator-terms), `p_norm=1`, na ang ibig sabihin ay tinatantya ang error bilang:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\langle\\psi|\\Delta|\\psi\\rangle| \\leq \\sum_{P\\in\\mathcal{T}} |c_P|\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $\\psi$ ay ang quantum state, ang $\\Delta$ ay ang totoong pagkakaiba ng eksakto at na-truncate na observable (na hindi alam), ang $\\mathcal{T}$ ay ang set ng mga Pauli term na na-truncate, at ang $c_P$ ay ang coefficient ng Pauli term.\n"
"Ang inequality na ito ay isang mahigpit ngunit napaluwag na upper bound sa karamihan ng mga sitwasyon.\n"
"Sa gabay na ito, bina-backpropagate ang anim na slice ng halimbawang circuit, gamit ang pare-parehong error kada slice na `0.001`. Ang halagang ito ay dapat unawain bilang budget sa loob ng ibinigay na `p_norm`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can now compute the expectation value of the backpropagated observable, as well as the error with respect to the exact reference:\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay maaari na nating kalkulahin ang expectation value ng na-backpropagate na observable, pati na ang error kumpara sa eksaktong reference:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we can plot the error incurred during the backpropagation of each slice, as well as the accumulated error.\n"
"The accumulated error is the sum of the slice errors. We can see that the accumulated error is a very loose upper bound to the actual error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Panghuli, maaari nating i-plot ang error na naipon sa backpropagation ng bawat slice, pati na ang naipon na kabuuang error.\n"
"Ang naipon na error ay ang kabuuan ng mga error ng bawat slice. Makikita natin na ang naipon na error ay isang napaluwag na upper bound sa totoong error.\n"

